From d3782f7636e7b4e533bffd6e5c924dc993d8b84a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:26:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 29/40] fix(core): cancel stale timers on exit and accept a
 timer only on its owner message (CC-01/ET-02)

A timer started under an older document version stayed in the snapshot
forever (exit cancelled only the timers of the current message as the NEW
document declares them) and its fire, with a valid token, could trigger an
arrow on a message that does not own the timer (section/root handler).

* Core/Chart `fire`: after the exit actions, cancel every snapshot timer
  that exit does not cancel (`staleCancels`; empty within one version).
* Core/Chart `step`: a timer event is accepted only if the current
  message owns the timer (`ownsTimer`, i.e. exit cancels it).
* Engine.missing, Trace.guardNames/firedIndex: same acceptance rule, so
  no `need` is asked for an event that will be ignored.
* Proof repairs (statements unchanged): compile_correct rewrites
  exitOf = exitActs before splitting on the acceptance test;
  step_snapOK covers the extra cancel actions.

Patch: agents/core-compiler/.../proposed_fix_UNVERIFIED.patch (core-compiler),
Engine/Trace parts and proof repairs by the integration agent; verified
on the from-source Lean 4.35.0 toolchain. bin/ not regenerated.

Docs: README decisions 2 and 7, FORMAT.md section 7 rule 2 and the HOST.md section 6
timers bullet (998a539 described the unfixed engine) now state the fixed behaviour.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
